## What I do with your answers

I read every response myself. Your answers shape what I bring up with the HPC teams at DTU, NGC,
and Gefion, what we prioritise when partitions are renewed, and which topics we turn into
[events](/events/) and training. One conversation tells me about one person's work; lots of answers
together show me what many of you are running into.

If it sounds like a chat would help more than a form, I'll reach out.

## Other ways to reach me

You never have to fill in a form to get help. The survey is just one way to reach me.

### Book a conversation

Grab a slot in my calendar and we'll meet in person or online, whichever suits you. Bring whatever
is on your mind: what you're trying to run, which cluster fits, why your jobs are slower than they
should be, or how to spend a hardware budget before you commit to it. It's part of my job, and it's
free.

<BookConsultation />

### Email or Slack

Email me at [bstja@dtu.dk](mailto:bstja@dtu.dk), or find the compute community in
`#compute` and `#ask-compute` on the P1 Slack.

